# Native pair stabilizer words

Five words in the certified Mathieu star generators fix both binary masks
818 and 1449. Their short products realize 96 distinct permutations. This
lower bound will identify the whole ambient pair centralizer by comparison
with the independent first-centralizer census.

The words were discovered with GAP from the existing native ATLAS generators;
Lean checks each permutation, its action on the kernel, and distinctness.
These are native markings, not an identification of the printed MOG labels.
Source motivation: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Section 2.1, pp.488--489.
-/
